1
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:06,000
National Radio and Television Administration.

2
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Welcome to Sister Pang's Bathhouse.

3
00:01:39,440 --> 00:01:40,759
Mr. Han, Mrs. Han.

4
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:43,729
I have to be honest with you.

5
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:46,570
This is my first time handling an insurance case.

6
00:01:47,680 --> 00:01:49,160
Although it's her first time,

7
00:01:49,160 --> 00:01:50,440
with Lawyer Xiao's

8
00:01:50,440 --> 00:01:51,520
professional ability,

9
00:01:51,520 --> 00:01:53,400
she can handle all types of cases.

10
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:56,520
Mr. Dong said you've handled many big cases.

11
00:01:56,520 --> 00:01:57,320
Our case

12
00:01:57,320 --> 00:01:59,039
shouldn't be a problem for you.

13
00:01:59,039 --> 00:01:59,840
Mr. Dong.

14
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:10,120
The main thing is I have to be responsible for you.

15
00:02:10,120 --> 00:02:12,120
Lawyer Xiao, please,

16
00:02:14,040 --> 00:02:16,640
try your best to fight for us.

17
00:02:17,440 --> 00:02:18,700
I just want this matter

18
00:02:20,079 --> 00:02:22,010
to be resolved as soon as possible.

19
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:28,760
Bowen, you've handled insurance cases before, right?

20
00:02:28,760 --> 00:02:30,920
Yes, I did a few before joining your team.

21
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:32,800
I represented the insurance companies.

22
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:33,680
Didn't you lose all of them?

23
00:02:33,680 --> 00:02:34,480
Shut up.

24
00:02:35,040 --> 00:02:36,280
You just have to talk, don't you?

25
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:38,680
Isn't failed experience still experience?

26
00:02:38,680 --> 00:02:39,840
That's why I always say,

27
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:42,120
it's hard for insurance companies nowadays.

28
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:43,560
I saw online

29
00:02:43,640 --> 00:02:44,920
that because the economy is bad,

30
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:47,480
more and more people are committing insurance fraud.

31
00:02:47,480 --> 00:02:50,000
After all, human nature can't stand the test.

32
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,480
So now the law on personal accident insurance stipulates

33
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:55,040
that the maximum payout for children under ten is 200,000 yuan.

34
00:02:55,040 --> 00:02:55,800
Exactly.

35
00:02:56,040 --> 00:02:58,040
Having a child costs tens of thousands now.

36
00:02:58,040 --> 00:03:00,480
If the child suddenly dies in an accident,

37
00:03:00,840 --> 00:03:03,080
they could get hundreds of thousands or even a million.

38
00:03:03,080 --> 00:03:05,880
Many people can't resist that kind of temptation.

39
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:08,040
Have you seen that video online?

40
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:10,080
It's about a couple getting on a ship.

41
00:03:10,080 --> 00:03:11,960
They were so loving. They went on a trip,

42
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:13,800
and as soon as they got on the deck, the man

43
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:14,600
pushed the woman off.

44
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:16,880
Lawyer Li, what do you think of this case?

45
00:03:20,720 --> 00:03:22,650
We are currently on the defensive.

46
00:03:23,320 --> 00:03:25,520
The other side is likely to attack from anywhere.

47
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:26,600
So our team

48
00:03:27,120 --> 00:03:29,079
needs to study the insurance contract carefully

49
00:03:29,079 --> 00:03:30,840
to see what weak points they might target.

50
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:31,800
Understood, Lawyer Li.

51
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:33,240
I will definitely perform well this time.

52
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:34,370
Meeting adjourned.

53
00:03:35,600 --> 00:03:36,720
What were you just saying?

54
00:03:36,720 --> 00:03:38,640
You really haven't seen that video?

55
00:03:38,640 --> 00:03:40,040
I'll send you that video.

56
00:03:53,440 --> 00:03:54,200
What are you doing?

57
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:55,440
Delivering water.

58
00:03:55,520 --> 00:03:56,440
So many words.

59
00:03:56,760 --> 00:03:57,160
It's fine.

60
00:03:57,160 --> 00:03:58,240
This insurance company

61
00:03:58,240 --> 00:03:59,000
is the best at making a scene.

62
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:00,680
We'll definitely crush them once we make a move.

63
00:04:00,680 --> 00:04:02,320
Stop making a fuss here.

64
00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:03,200
It's so annoying.

65
00:04:03,200 --> 00:04:04,200
Don't be annoyed.

66
00:04:04,440 --> 00:04:06,440
Who asked us to be top players in the legal field?

67
00:04:06,440 --> 00:04:08,840
With great power comes great responsibility.

68
00:04:08,840 --> 00:04:10,400
Are you trying to flatter me to death?

69
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:11,840
This is all from the bottom of my heart.

70
00:04:11,840 --> 00:04:13,320
What do you mean by excessive praise?

71
00:04:13,320 --> 00:04:14,000
Give it a rest.

72
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:14,840
If you ask me,

73
00:04:15,040 --> 00:04:17,320
if even Sister Long can't win this case,

74
00:04:17,320 --> 00:04:18,480
then anyone else would lose too.

75
00:04:18,480 --> 00:04:19,440
Have some sunflower seeds.

76
00:04:19,440 --> 00:04:21,279
Look at the bad habit you've given him.

77
00:04:21,279 --> 00:04:22,480
He just opens his mouth and flatters.

78
00:04:22,480 --> 00:04:23,680
Are you sincere?

79
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:25,360
Yes, absolutely sincere.

80
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:27,360
Lawyer Xiao definitely won't lose.

81
00:04:28,760 --> 00:04:32,080
Besides, insurance cases favor the policyholder.

82
00:04:33,720 --> 00:04:35,520
According to the Insurance Law of the People's Republic of China,

83
00:04:35,520 --> 00:04:36,520
Article 30,

84
00:04:36,640 --> 00:04:38,520
if standard clauses provided by the insurer are used

85
00:04:38,520 --> 00:04:39,840
to conclude an insurance contract,

86
00:04:39,840 --> 00:04:41,440
and the insurer and the policyholder,

87
00:04:41,440 --> 00:04:43,120
the insured or the beneficiary

88
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:44,640
have a dispute over the contract clauses,

89
00:04:44,640 --> 00:04:46,640
they shall be interpreted according to common understanding.

90
00:04:46,640 --> 00:04:48,960
If there are two or more interpretations of the contract clauses,

91
00:04:48,960 --> 00:04:51,360
the people's court or arbitration institution shall make

92
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:54,890
an interpretation in favor of the insured and the beneficiary.

93
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:05,000
Not bad. You memorized it.

94
00:05:05,240 --> 00:05:08,040
Uncle, I can memorize even longer ones.

95
00:05:08,160 --> 00:05:09,440
Then do another one.

96
00:05:09,440 --> 00:05:12,160
How about Article 600 of the Criminal Law?

97
00:05:15,280 --> 00:05:18,440
There are 452 articles in the Criminal Law.

98
00:05:18,760 --> 00:05:20,040
You read the Criminal Law every day.

99
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:21,160
Didn't you count how many articles there are?

100
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:22,840
No, I didn't read to the end.

101
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:24,640
I was just bluffing.

102
00:05:24,640 --> 00:05:26,320
I wanted to see how well you know it.

103
00:05:26,320 --> 00:05:27,440
You're good.

104
00:05:27,760 --> 00:05:28,840
Was what he just said correct?

105
00:05:28,840 --> 00:05:30,000
Yes, definitely.

106
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:30,480
He memorized it

107
00:05:30,480 --> 00:05:31,640
like an AI.

108
00:05:31,640 --> 00:05:34,100
But it doesn't completely apply to our case.

109
00:05:35,320 --> 00:05:36,880
I'll look into it more.

110
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:39,320
Luo Zhi, you memorized it well.

111
00:05:39,520 --> 00:05:40,320
Let's go, sis.

112
00:05:48,080 --> 00:05:50,720
Not bad. You don't wear glasses for nothing.

113
00:05:56,760 --> 00:05:58,560
You're pretty good.

114
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:01,530
Your movements are a bit exaggerated.

115
00:06:04,520 --> 00:06:06,040
Where are you?

116
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:08,600
Sorry, I'm late.

117
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:10,200
Lawyer Xiao.

118
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:11,520
You're late.

119
00:06:11,520 --> 00:06:12,200
We were waiting for you. Come, take the seat of honor.

120
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:13,320
Sit down.

121
00:06:13,640 --> 00:06:14,640
What do you mean?

122
00:06:15,040 --> 00:06:16,370
Are you asking me to pay?

123
00:06:16,880 --> 00:06:18,440
You're the star who arrived last.

124
00:06:18,440 --> 00:06:20,040
How could I let you pay? I'll pay.

125
00:06:20,040 --> 00:06:22,240
Right. You drive a Benz. You should pay.

126
00:06:23,200 --> 00:06:24,200
Thanks, Lawyer Li.

127
00:06:24,200 --> 00:06:25,660
Here. I didn't add garlic.

128
00:06:28,200 --> 00:06:31,520
Since Lawyer Li is paying, I'll order some good wine.

129
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:34,659
Drink less, or you'll have a headache tomorrow.

130
00:06:34,720 --> 00:06:35,920
Drink more hot water.

131
00:06:36,640 --> 00:06:37,520
You really are...

132
00:06:37,520 --> 00:06:39,840
How many years have you two been married?

133
00:06:39,960 --> 00:06:42,040
Why are you being so affectionate today?

134
00:06:42,040 --> 00:06:42,840
Are you putting on a show for us?

135
00:06:42,840 --> 00:06:43,720
Is it any of your business?

136
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:45,440
Are you trying to make us jealous?

137
00:06:45,440 --> 00:06:46,400
Let me tell you.

138
00:06:46,440 --> 00:06:48,840
This guy had a crush on Zhao Jia in school.

139
00:06:49,080 --> 00:06:50,720
But Cheng Fei beat him to it.

140
00:06:50,720 --> 00:06:51,360
Lian.

141
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:53,800
You never told me about this.

142
00:06:53,880 --> 00:06:54,360
No.

143
00:06:54,640 --> 00:06:55,440
Lawyer Li.

144
00:06:55,440 --> 00:06:56,840
I'm suing her for defamation.

145
00:06:56,840 --> 00:06:57,600
Go ahead.

146
00:06:57,680 --> 00:06:58,400
I'm not afraid of you.

147
00:06:58,400 --> 00:07:00,200
I have our Lawyer Xiao.

148
00:07:00,400 --> 00:07:01,440
Old classmates are the best.

149
00:07:01,440 --> 00:07:02,520
Introducing business to me right away.

150
00:07:02,520 --> 00:07:03,760
But I charge legal fees.

151
00:07:03,760 --> 00:07:04,400
Of course.

152
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:05,930
Just give me a 20% discount.

153
00:07:06,080 --> 00:07:07,720
What cases are you two working on lately?

154
00:07:07,720 --> 00:07:08,840
An insurance case.

155
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:20,160
Your client wouldn't happen to be Shengkang Insurance, would it?

156
00:07:21,440 --> 00:07:23,370
Then your client's surname is Han.

157
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:24,920
Really?

158
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:28,080
How could this...

159
00:07:28,080 --> 00:07:30,080
You're debating again, aren't you?

160
00:07:30,800 --> 00:07:32,280
What did they argue about when they were in school?

161
00:07:32,280 --> 00:07:33,280
Whether that circle was round or not.

162
00:07:33,280 --> 00:07:34,480
Anyway, I remember it very clearly.

163
00:07:34,480 --> 00:07:37,680
Li Xin said there is no perfect circle in the world.

164
00:07:38,080 --> 00:07:41,200
Xiao went to the blackboard and drew a circle by hand.

165
00:07:41,200 --> 00:07:43,040
That circle looked like it was drawn with a compass.

166
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:44,840
I wasn't talking about whether it was round or not.

167
00:07:44,840 --> 00:07:45,720
What I meant was,

168
00:07:45,720 --> 00:07:48,200
there is no absolute fairness and justice in this world,

169
00:07:48,200 --> 00:07:49,080
just like there is no

170
00:07:49,080 --> 00:07:50,320
perfect circle in this world.

171
00:07:50,320 --> 00:07:51,580
Then she just had to...

172
00:07:51,640 --> 00:07:54,440
You said that, so what if I draw you another circle?

173
00:07:54,560 --> 00:07:55,280
Some things,

174
00:07:55,280 --> 00:07:57,200
as long as we pursue them, they exist.

175
00:07:57,200 --> 00:07:57,960
Right?

176
00:07:57,960 --> 00:07:58,560
Yes.

177
00:07:58,560 --> 00:07:59,720
Can you draw it rounder than this pot?

178
00:07:59,720 --> 00:08:01,600
Then tell me, is this a perfect circle?

179
00:08:01,600 --> 00:08:02,720
I'm talking about objectivity.

180
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:03,400
How is it objective?

181
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:05,080
Is it an objective circle?

182
00:08:05,080 --> 00:08:05,840
It's subjective.

183
00:08:05,840 --> 00:08:06,800
How is it subjective?

184
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:07,680
It was made.

185
00:08:07,720 --> 00:08:08,640
Excuse me.

186
00:08:09,080 --> 00:08:10,200
I have a question.

187
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:11,720
It's been bothering me until now.

188
00:08:11,720 --> 00:08:12,840
It's been bothering me since high school.

189
00:08:12,840 --> 00:08:14,280
What is it?

190
00:08:14,520 --> 00:08:15,760
Did you two ever date?

191
00:08:19,400 --> 00:08:20,600
No.

192
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:21,520
Impossible. Look.

193
00:08:21,520 --> 00:08:22,520
They won't admit it.

194
00:08:22,520 --> 00:08:24,720
A guilty conscience needs no accuser, right?

195
00:08:24,720 --> 00:08:25,440
But when we were in school,

196
00:08:25,440 --> 00:08:27,600
I thought you two were a perfect match.

197
00:08:27,600 --> 00:08:28,400
No, Zhao Jia.

198
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:30,440
You still look like a perfect match now.

199
00:08:30,440 --> 00:08:31,880
Yes, we all think so.

200
00:08:31,880 --> 00:08:32,760
Zhao Jia,

201
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:35,280
what could you see when you were in school?

202
00:08:35,280 --> 00:08:37,340
Weren't you highly myopic back then?

203
00:08:37,840 --> 00:08:38,200
Exactly.

204
00:08:38,200 --> 00:08:39,840
Otherwise, how could she have fallen for Cheng Fei?

205
00:08:39,840 --> 00:08:40,919
Come on.

206
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:41,880
Come on.

207
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:42,880
Come on.

208
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:45,000
Let's see which of you two

209
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:46,560
can win this case, right?

210
00:08:47,320 --> 00:08:48,840
Lian, you have to treat me to a meal.

211
00:08:48,840 --> 00:08:50,280
No problem, my treat.

212
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:52,140
I only found out about this today.

213
00:08:57,400 --> 00:08:59,840
My nephew is so capable.

214
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:01,200
Uncle, I'm fast.

215
00:09:01,280 --> 00:09:02,560
Stop working. Come here.

216
00:09:02,560 --> 00:09:04,000
Let me chat with you. Come.

217
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:04,320
Sit.

218
00:09:07,480 --> 00:09:08,680
You're so lovable.

219
00:09:11,240 --> 00:09:11,640
No.

220
00:09:11,640 --> 00:09:14,200
What's wrong, Uncle? You're scaring me by looking at me like that.

221
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:16,600
What are you afraid of? Am I going to eat you?

222
00:09:18,280 --> 00:09:20,840
This skill of memorizing laws,

223
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:22,570
why didn't you show it earlier?

224
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:25,040
Uncle, I...

225
00:09:25,080 --> 00:09:26,400
The day you picked me up at the train station,

226
00:09:26,400 --> 00:09:28,720
I told you I had a good memory. Did you forget?

227
00:09:28,720 --> 00:09:30,440
You said it so subtly.

228
00:09:30,760 --> 00:09:32,640
That was close. We almost missed this opportunity.

229
00:09:32,640 --> 00:09:34,960
Alright, you've passed my test.

230
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:36,400
Really, Uncle?

231
00:09:36,400 --> 00:09:37,840
Would I lie to you?

232
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:40,400
Now, we just need Xiao Longnv to nod.

233
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:42,880
I'll create more opportunities for you.

234
00:09:42,880 --> 00:09:44,040
When you get the chance,

235
00:09:44,040 --> 00:09:46,080
you should show off well, okay?

236
00:09:46,200 --> 00:09:46,880
Okay.

237
00:09:46,880 --> 00:09:47,840
Don't forget.

238
00:09:47,880 --> 00:09:50,610
Whose side are you on after entering the law firm?

239
00:09:51,720 --> 00:09:52,720
I won't forget.

240
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:54,180
I'm on the law firm's side.

241
00:09:55,160 --> 00:09:56,400
You're on my side.

242
00:09:56,640 --> 00:09:57,760
Dong Beihu's side.

243
00:09:58,640 --> 00:09:59,400
Understand?

244
00:10:00,280 --> 00:10:01,840
Understood. We're related by blood.

245
00:10:01,840 --> 00:10:02,400
Right.

246
00:10:02,400 --> 00:10:02,960
Bye.

247
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:04,640
My treat next time. Old Lian, my treat.

248
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:05,400
It's settled then.

249
00:10:05,400 --> 00:10:06,040
Okay.

250
00:10:06,280 --> 00:10:06,920
Bye.

251
00:10:06,920 --> 00:10:08,160
I'm taking the drunk girl home.

252
00:10:08,160 --> 00:10:08,880
Bye. Bye. Let's go.

253
00:10:08,880 --> 00:10:09,520
Bye.

254
00:10:09,560 --> 00:10:10,560
Drive slowly.

255
00:10:13,760 --> 00:10:15,280
Let's go. I'll take you back.

256
00:10:15,280 --> 00:10:17,640
No, we're opponents now.

257
00:10:17,680 --> 00:10:18,520
Keep some

258
00:10:18,520 --> 00:10:20,160
distance that opponents should have.

259
00:10:20,160 --> 00:10:21,040
All right.

260
00:10:21,880 --> 00:10:24,160
See you in court then.

261
00:10:25,160 --> 00:10:26,920
Let's have a good match.

262
00:10:27,560 --> 00:10:29,680
Don't worry, I won't show any mercy.

263
00:10:31,680 --> 00:10:32,740
What are you doing?

264
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:34,160
Nothing.

265
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:37,640
You're so annoying.

266
00:10:43,560 --> 00:10:44,760
What are you doing?

267
00:10:45,280 --> 00:10:47,080
Lawyer Xiao is so busy every day.

268
00:10:47,840 --> 00:10:50,400
Are insurance cases that easy to win?

269
00:10:50,680 --> 00:10:51,880
What did you find?

270
00:10:52,280 --> 00:10:55,000
Documents? This must have taken a lot of effort.

271
00:10:55,280 --> 00:10:55,880
What nonsense.

272
00:10:55,880 --> 00:10:58,520
You'd even die to work with Lawyer Xiao?

273
00:10:58,560 --> 00:10:59,920
Don't say that, kid.

274
00:11:00,160 --> 00:11:01,090
Come in quickly.

275
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:03,680
What kind of act are you putting on here?

276
00:11:03,680 --> 00:11:04,160
No, no.

277
00:11:04,160 --> 00:11:05,800
Luo Zhi is so enthusiastic about his work.

278
00:11:05,800 --> 00:11:06,760
I couldn't stop him. Hurry.

279
00:11:06,760 --> 00:11:07,620
